{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01PbFpr3MX8vRGkpzSNTJZAH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Here's what was written for **Q8: Measure hallucination rate in production?**\n\n---\n\n**Key points in the answer:**\n\n1. **Define operationally** — RAGAS faithfulness (< 0.80 = hallucination) or NLI entailment per-sentence (NEUTRAL/CONTRADICTION fraction), not just \"user reports it wrong\"\n\n2. **Async pipeline architecture** — log `{run_id, query, context_chunks, response}` to Kafka at generation time → offline consumer runs DeBERTa NLI scoring → metrics emitted to Datadog with < 5 min lag. Never block the user path.\n\n3. **Two-track scoring** — NLI on 100% of traffic (~$120/day for 200K queries on an A10 sidecar), GPT-4o-mini LLM-judge on 5–10% for root-cause explainability (~$60/day)\n\n4. **SLO + alerting** — faithfulness p50 ≥ 0.92, rolling 7-day hallucination rate ≤ 3%; PagerDuty alert on 15 min breach\n\n5. **Segment by root cause** — break by retrieval cosine score band, query category, model version (retrieval failure vs generation drift)\n\n**3 pitfalls flagged:** treating it as one-time offline eval; proposing synchronous NLI blocking user responses; reporting a single global rate without segmentation."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":269,"cache_read_input_tokens":66876,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":269,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0f01f59e-5194-4acc-8485-d516d8818c63","uuid":"a15ee7b3-852a-402e-a322-89973c951f64"}
